		{"id":"3fb86030a91485d4","type":"text","text":"Draw curve","x":-5086,"y":3080,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"9a640c701611862d","type":"text","text":"Example 3 (file: SurfaceTurbulence):\n* Create sourcing geometry and initial attribs (Cd, N, v, etc.)\n\t* IMPORTANT: attribute v: sourcing geometry was used to compute vector field (v) which is further used for driving particles inside POP Net using POP VOP\n* Use POP Net for particle system\n* Use Point VOP to drive particles using vector field computed from sourcing geometry\n* Use POP Force with noise to make flow turbulent\n*  After POP Net, use particles to form trails","x":-5875,"y":1963,"width":807,"height":277},
		{"id":"86a3328686f128e7","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/4/CurveGuide2.png","x":-4475,"y":2714,"width":550,"height":363},
		{"id":"415eb2a9792297df","type":"text","text":"Example 4: (file: CurveGuideCollision):\n* Create sourcing geometry and initial attribs (Cd, N, etc.)\n* Create curve geometry which will be later used inside POP Net for guiding particles\n* Use POP Net for particle system\n* Use POP Curve Force node to drive particles using vector field created from curve geometry\n* Optional:\n\t* Use POP Collision Detect\n\t* Use POP stream for spawning sub-particle-system\n* After POP Net, use particles to form trails","x":-5900,"y":2715,"width":757,"height":365},
		{"id":"fd1c7f538b3442bb","type":"text","text":"POP Net particle system:\n* Curl vector field\n* Raycast solver","x":-3656,"y":1524,"width":250,"height":116},
		{"id":"620bd5e8d6624659","type":"text","text":"Display","x":-3174,"y":1524,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"19eab75c97b159d4","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/SurfaceFlow6.png","x":-2696,"y":1150,"width":400,"height":374},
		{"id":"bc9fd3b3b7444bf0","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/points.jpg","x":-2110,"y":1157,"width":652,"height":367},
		{"id":"fe8a8b39bbff3404","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/SurfaceFlow4.png","x":-3656,"y":1150,"width":400,"height":374},
		{"id":"cd2909f0376c2428","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/SurfaceFlow5.png","x":-3174,"y":1150,"width":400,"height":374},
		{"id":"ea36548fb926cfb9","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/SurfaceFlow2.png","x":-4567,"y":1150,"width":400,"height":374},
		{"id":"59c875b8e9ed0a64","type":"text","text":"Particle advection by volume vector field\n\nExample:\n1. Mesh is used to generate main shape (only surface).\n2. Differential geometry OPs are used to compute information per surface points (e.g., tangent field)\n3. Surface is rasterized into volume grid where each cell is assigned with vector value\n4. Particle simulation is using volume grid information for movement.\n\nExample:\n1. Mesh is used to generate main shape (only surface).\n2. Mesh is rasterized: converted to grid\n3. Noise is computed for each grid cell resulting in volume vector field\n4. Particle simulation is using volume grid information for movement.\n\nTutorials:\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JS3rw7W1gN4\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rC9EGQJOLyE\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WKDY5b_V5go\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K0cNvpXujmk","x":-420,"y":1340,"width":790,"height":660},
		{"id":"2db206698c738cc7","type":"text","text":"Initial attributes","x":-4567,"y":1524,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c7f03e4dc55f609e","type":"text","text":"POP Net particle system","x":-4116,"y":1524,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"247c39d1732b7fc7","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/SurfaceFlow3.png","x":-4116,"y":1150,"width":400,"height":374},
		{"id":"fecc586236fd1f76","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8OXb5GjRrTo","x":-475,"y":3281,"width":655,"height":394},
		{"id":"974b4a4b3b6ae865","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FBP9k6W48vM","x":-475,"y":2851,"width":655,"height":360},
		{"id":"3a5dd3a28d801052","type":"link","url":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/ParticleSystems.html","x":-475,"y":2311,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"71293dd4e4f4817d","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/3/SurfaceFlow1.png","x":-5021,"y":1150,"width":400,"height":374},
