		{"id":"4003a76034293565","type":"text","text":"Initial attributes","x":-4685,"y":651,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"12e7af9151f4a3c4","type":"text","text":"Masking","x":-4231,"y":651,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"767ec30828baf323","type":"text","text":"* **Particle systems are quite often created in target environment** - transferring particles between DCCs and game engines is often not possible in desired extent (e.g., Blender and Unity)\n* **Each DCC or Game engine has its own particle system implementation** (although they are all quite similar)\n* **A standardization for transfer between DCCs and Game engines doesn't exist**\n\n\n\n\n","x":-8037,"y":-1,"width":884,"height":175},
		{"id":"8b8fc35e742a0ed0","type":"text","text":"If target is game in **Godot**, then Godot's particle system will be used.","x":-7788,"y":478,"width":386,"height":102},
		{"id":"5eebcd8dc29b904f","type":"link","url":"https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/latest/modeling/geometry_nodes/introduction.html","x":-7322,"y":1124,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2c1d0c4e8778064d","type":"link","url":"https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/latest/physics/particles/introduction.html","x":-7322,"y":665,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2a3c51542fe0912d","type":"text","text":"If target is motion graphics animation is **Houdini**, then Houdini POP (DOP/SOP) will be used","x":-6842,"y":486,"width":400,"height":110},
		{"id":"6f6bc63a194dd76f","type":"link","url":"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/2d/particle_systems_2d.html","x":-7788,"y":665,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d820f347bafcac63","type":"text","text":"Sourcing geometry","x":-5138,"y":651,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"079e7781767b3b6d","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/2/VectorFieldGuideSrc1.png","x":-5138,"y":296,"width":400,"height":355},
		{"id":"07440970d37a679d","type":"text","text":"Example 1 (file: VectorFieldSourcing):\n* Create sourcing geometry and initial attribs (Cd, N, etc.)\n* Use POP Net for particle system\n* Inside POP Net use Geometry/Point VOP to drive particles using noise vector field\n*  After POP Net, use particles to form trails","x":-5882,"y":402,"width":680,"height":180},
		{"id":"42feb67cae7ff8d9","type":"link","url":"https://www.gamedeveloper.com/programming/building-an-advanced-particle-system","x":1670,"y":31,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"562f4ab8ecfb7959","type":"text","text":"If target is animated film in **Blender**, then Blender Particle System or Geometry nodes will be used.","x":-7322,"y":477,"width":400,"height":119},
		{"id":"83030c39cac7e52b","type":"text","text":"Various vector field guides","x":-2043,"y":31,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"641a49f37d1dc5b3","type":"text","text":"If target is game in **Unreal**, then Unreal Niagara will be used.","x":-8228,"y":477,"width":400,"height":103},
		{"id":"49e2c9a8a68ad502","type":"link","url":"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/creating-visual-effects-in-niagara-for-unreal-engine","x":-8228,"y":665,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"6933d46c60ef1035","type":"link","url":"https://discussions.unity.com/t/new-free-e-book-the-definitive-guide-to-creating-advanced-visual-effects-in-unity-unity-6-edition/1563811","x":1890,"y":2311,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d5c1d891b931d119","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/Concepts/ParticleSystem_4.png","x":-9675,"y":320,"width":400,"height":376},
		{"id":"0b119e24ac3df365","type":"text","text":"If target is game in **Unity**, then Unity VFX Graph or Built-in particle system will be used.","x":-8668,"y":477,"width":400,"height":103},
