		{"id":"3c26ac655ad6270f","type":"text","text":"Convert particles to volume and rendering:\n* https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/42457/\n* Volume rasterize particles: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterizeparticles.html\n* Volume rasterize points: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterizepoints.html\n* Volume rasterize attributes: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/volumerasterizeattributes.html + https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0SDptfygg\n* Volume color: https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/53590/?page=1#post-351635 + https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/sop/paintcolorvolume.html","x":-3635,"y":8065,"width":700,"height":367},
		{"id":"03498f8473a7cc63","type":"text","text":"Example 2 (VolumeMorphing2)","x":-5920,"y":8065,"width":359,"height":93},
		{"id":"86ff4c6ca98de0cb","type":"text","text":"particle system advect by volumes - feedback loop:\n* https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/dop/popadvectbyvolumes.html","x":-3116,"y":4114,"width":320,"height":168},
		{"id":"4ec8099cd06b2495","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/VolumeField2.png","x":-4731,"y":3842,"width":400,"height":313},
		{"id":"84a7667f18bf36f3","type":"text","text":"Geometry tangent field stored in voxel grid (Volume VOP with PC Open and Filter)","x":-4065,"y":3966,"width":392,"height":114},
		{"id":"918bd9823e289628","type":"text","text":"Example 5 (file: ParticlesVolumeAdvect):\n* Create sourcing geometry, convert to volume and compute initial attribs \n\t* NOTE:  Particles will be spawned inside volume\n* Create curve and from it tube geometry, compute vector field using this geometry, store vector field in BB volume of this geometry\n* Use POP Net for particle system\n* Inside POP Net, use POP Advect By Volumes to drive particles using vector field computed  vector stored in volume\n* After POP Net, use particles to form trails\n* Optionally, convert particles from POP Net to volume and mesh","x":-5876,"y":3679,"width":757,"height":320},
		{"id":"97877b403da123ca","type":"text","text":"Volume as data structure for storing vector field for particles: rasterize volume of surface containing vector field and volume advect in POP for particle simulation\n\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0SDptfygg\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yqM_3goH4J8\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rn_8iN7lyjI\n","x":-4065,"y":4080,"width":700,"height":202},
		{"id":"f6fb2ba05cca1850","type":"text","text":"Geometry with computed  surface tangent field ","x":-4731,"y":4155,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"710fa593121a4305","type":"text","text":"Point Cloud Open and Point Cloud Filter VOP/VEX nodes/functions are used to access point information around current particle in POP VOP. This way, vector field stored at points can be used to drive particles.\n\nIt can be used for any kind of points in surface or volume:\n1. Surface points: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zJls__AJlJo\n2. Volume points: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JS3rw7W1gN4&t=11s ","x":-4065,"y":4282,"width":700,"height":231},
		{"id":"6d52b6b5da9319e8","type":"text","text":"Advection:\n\n* https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advection\n* In the fields of [physics](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physics \"Physics\"), [engineering](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Engineering \"Engineering\"), and [earth sciences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth_science \"Earth science\"), **advection** is the [transport](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transport \"Transport\") of a substance or quantity by bulk motion of a fluid.\n* During advection, a fluid transports some conserved quantity or material via bulk motion. The fluid's motion is described [mathematically](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics \"Mathematics\") as a [vector field](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vector_field \"Vector field\"), and the transported material is described by a [scalar field](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scalar_field \"Scalar field\") showing its distribution over space.","x":-3121,"y":4282,"width":710,"height":280},
		{"id":"46f0fbcf35151d85","type":"file","file":"Images/Fuzzy/LectureExamples/6/VolumesParticles2.jpg","x":-2560,"y":4717,"width":400,"height":247},
		{"id":"1fd0fb4d0fedad69","type":"text","text":"Convert volume to particles for artistic particle system morphing (advection) using volumetric vector field:\n* It is easier to model forces on particles and then to convert those to volume \n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WySzeEniScs\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wR0SDptfygg","x":-5259,"y":8065,"width":1008,"height":367},
		{"id":"ef6609870b62b613","type":"text","text":"Volume from particles:\n* VDB from particles \n* OR Volume rasterize attributes node\n","x":-3474,"y":8540,"width":380,"height":160},
